        <object label="&lt;b&gt;runEval() — 9 STEPS, complete, in code order · runner.js&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;1 load golden-set.json · 2 create judge (mock|real)&lt;br&gt;3 loop: ragSystem() → judge.evaluate()&lt;br&gt;4 computeAggregate — skips parseError rows&lt;br&gt;5 loadBaseline → detectRegressions&lt;br&gt;6 generateReport → writeReport&lt;br&gt;7 saveBaseline if --save-baseline OR no baseline&lt;br&gt;8 print aggregate + PASS/FAIL verdict&lt;br&gt;9 --ci AND hasRegressions → process.exit(1)" class="card.invariant" id="card_pipeline">
          <mxCell style="rounded=1;fillColor=#E8EAF6;strokeColor=#3F51B5;strokeWidth=1.5;fontSize=8;fontColor=#232F3E;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;spacingLeft=6;opacity=70;" parent="1" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry x="360" y="524" width="440" height="140" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </object>
        <object label="&lt;b&gt;REGRESSION GATES — every threshold, regression.js&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;REGRESSION_THRESHOLD_POINTS = 1 — per-dim drop&lt;br&gt;IMPROVEMENT_THRESHOLD_POINTS = 1 — per-dim gain&lt;br&gt;AGGREGATE_THRESHOLD_PERCENT = 0.05 — 5% drop&lt;br&gt;applied: diff &amp;lt; -1 → regressed&lt;br&gt;diff &amp;gt; +1 → improved · else unchanged&lt;br&gt;pctChange &amp;lt; -0.05 → aggregateRegression&lt;br&gt;hasRegressions = regressions.length &amp;gt; 0 OR agg&lt;br&gt;no baseline → false, and this run becomes the baseline" class="card.failure" id="card_gates">
          <mxCell style="rounded=1;fillColor=#FFEBEE;strokeColor=#C62828;strokeWidth=1.5;fontSize=8;fontColor=#232F3E;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;spacingLeft=6;opacity=70;" parent="1" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry x="824" y="524" width="440" height="140" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </object>
        <object label="&lt;b&gt;THE 3 DIMENSIONS — complete, in DIMENSIONS array order · dimensions.js&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;faithfulness w=0.4 — grounded in sources? prompt · rubric 5→1 · 4 calibrations&lt;br&gt;relevance w=0.3 — answers the question? prompt · rubric · 4 calibrations&lt;br&gt;completeness w=0.3 — covers all key points? prompt · rubric · 4 calibrations&lt;br&gt;composite sums only non-parseError dims · mock judge hard-codes the same weights&lt;br&gt;parseJudgeResponse — 3 exits to score 0: no JSON · out of 1-5 · throw" class="card.primitive" id="card_dims">
